Task: asyncApiGenerate task + Compile/compile chaining (Phase 4 of sbt-asyncapi-plugin_20261017)

Summary: Added AsyncApiHtmlGenerator (ports scripts/generate-kafka-asyncapi-docs.sh's
@asyncapi/cli@4.1.1 + patched @asyncapi/html-template@1.0.0 logic to plain
scala.sys.process calls - install-once-cache-under-target, patch
apiVersion v2->v3 once, clear+regenerate output dir without deleting it).
Node-toolchain failures are caught and warned (log.warn), never thrown.
Added asyncApiGenerate task wiring it in, and chained Compile/compile :=
{ val a = (Compile/compile).value; asyncApiGenerate.value; a } so every
`sbt kafkaHarness/compile` regenerates docs automatically.

MAJOR deviation found during this phase, requiring reopening Phase 3's
already-committed work: chaining asyncApiGenerate after Compile/compile
created a genuine circular task dependency, because asyncApiGenerateSpec
(Phase 3) used (Compile / runMain), which itself depends on (Compile /
compile) - compile -> asyncApiGenerate -> asyncApiGenerateSpec -> runMain ->
compile. Confirmed empirically: `sbt kafkaHarness/compile` hung indefinitely
rather than failing fast (sbt's static cyclic-reference detection doesn't
catch this because the dependency is wired through Def.taskDyn, resolved
dynamically at task-execution time, not statically at settings-load time).

Fix: rewrote asyncApiGenerateSpec to invoke AsyncApiSpecWriter via a direct
`java` subprocess, building its classpath from (Compile / classDirectory)
(a plain SettingKey, not compile-dependent) + (Compile / dependencyClasspath)
(depends only on upstream projects' exportedProducts/library resolution,
not this project's own compile) - neither depends on this project's own
Compile/compile task, breaking the cycle. Simpler than the original
Def.taskDyn/.toTask approach as a side benefit (no InputTask wrapping
needed at all).

Verified end-to-end: `sbt kafkaHarness/compile` alone (fresh run, no prior
asyncApiGenerateSpec/asyncApiGenerate run) produced
modules/kafka-harness/target/asyncapi-docs/index.html containing DemoEvent,
confirming this phase's own acceptance criterion exactly. Full `sbt compile
test` (0 failures) + scalafmtCheck on both plugin files clean.

